# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and deployed to Linux. Git's default
# on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout, which is harmless for source files
# and BREAKS anything the kernel has to interpret:
#
#   · a shell script with CRLF fails as `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`
#   · a Dockerfile RUN line carries the ^M into the shell it starts
#   · a systemd unit with CRLF is rejected as malformed
#
# Every one of those fails on the server, after a clean local test, with an
# error message that does not mention line endings. So: text is normalised to
# LF in the repository, and the files that must stay LF on disk say so.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed on Linux — never CRLF, on any platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
*.caddy         text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
*.env.example   text eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.dump binary
